    "text": "In a magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.05</mn><mtext>&nbsp;T</mtext></math>, area of a coil changes from <math> <mrow> <mn>101</mn><msup> <mrow> <mtext>&nbsp;cm</mtext></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math> to <math> <mrow> <mn>100</mn><msup> <mrow> <mtext>&nbsp;cm</mtext></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math> without changing the resistance which is <math> <mrow> <mn>2&nbsp;</mn><mn>Ω</mn></mrow></math>. The amount of charge (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>) that flows during this period is",
